A||N||26||Phil||Eating New Years cookies||||1||
Z||000000||Phil||01-03-2000||12:07 PM||||This is slightly off topic but it still is forum based. Maybe some of you computer G's can help me out. It seems that this forum won't set cookies on my computer any more. I've tried the cookie reset deal under preferences no help. I've deleted all the cookie files and then went to some different sites and again looked at my cookie file and sho nuff there were entries but none for the Forum. If I don't exit Netscape 4.7 and return to the Forum at a later time all the little lights and candles work fine but if I shut Netscape down and then fire up and return to the Forum no lights, candles or last visit setting. I guess Cliff dosen't like me any more. Can any body think if a way I can outfox Cliff. This all started yesterday afternoon. Y2K Y2K Y2k!!!!!! Panic||||reg||1
Z||000001||Cliff Pennock||01-03-2000||12:50 PM||||  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Don't worry Phil, I still like you (this doesn't mean we're married or anything!).<P>I'm not sure what the problem could be with the cookies. The forum's software is Y2K-proof, and so is the server it is running on.<P>The only reason I can think of that cookies are only <I>remembered</I> during the current session, is because of a Y2K related problem on <B>your</B> side... A cookie has a certain expiration date. For some reason the cookie expires as soon as you leave Netscape. I would suggest you not only check the date in Windows, but in your computer's BIOS as well (these are two seperate clocks!).<P>To get into the BIOS of your computer, you have to watch your screen carefully when you switch it on. You always get a message similar to "Press &lt;DEL&gt; for SETUP". When you see this message, press the appropriate key. This will start the BIOS Setup. <B>Be careful though! You could easily mess up your computer if you change something here!</B> So if you're not certain of how to check/change the system's date, better get someone who does to do it for you.<P>Good luck!<p>[This message has been edited by Cliff Pennock (edited 01-03-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Phil||01-03-2000||01:02 PM||||Checked both clocks and both are correct. Oh well. Anybody else? ||||reg||8
